<article class="env-lemma" id="036C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/036C">Lemma <span data-tag="036C">35.18.3</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(S) =$“$S$ is locally Noetherian and $(R_ k)$” is local in the smooth topology. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will check (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0349" data-tag="0349">35.15.2</a>. As a smooth morphism is flat of finite presentation (Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/01VF" data-tag="01VF">29.35.9</a> and <a href="/tag/01VE" data-tag="01VE">29.35.8</a>) we have already checked this for “being locally Noetherian” in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/034C" data-tag="034C">35.16.1</a>. We will use this without further mention in the proof. First we note that $\mathcal{P}$ is local in the Zariski topology. This is clear from the definition, see Properties, Definition <a href="/tag/033Q" data-tag="033Q">28.12.1</a>. Next, we show that if $S' \to S$ is a smooth morphism of affines and $S$ has $\mathcal{P}$, then $S'$ has $\mathcal{P}$. This is Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/033A" data-tag="033A">10.163.5</a> (use Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01V6" data-tag="01V6">29.35.2</a>, Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/00T4" data-tag="00T4">10.137.3</a> and <a href="/tag/00TT" data-tag="00TT">10.140.3</a>). Finally, we show that if $S' \to S$ is a surjective smooth morphism of affines and $S'$ has $\mathcal{P}$, then $S$ has $\mathcal{P}$. This is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0353" data-tag="0353">10.164.6</a>. Thus (1), (2) and (3) of Lemma <a href="/tag/0349" data-tag="0349">35.15.2</a> hold and we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>